+Tool: built-in image_gen image-edit calls, generated sequentially with refs/background.png as the base reference.
+Finalization: generated botanical pixels isolated from the model sky, placed over the original 2880x1800 screenshot, with geometry adjusted to the requested reach and exclusion zones. Native generated drafts were 1586x992; the botanical content was resized during compositing. Original screenshot pixels were retained outside the new botanical layer. Rejected drafts are not included in v2.
+
+01 Classic
+Edit the first image, a CERNAN website screenshot. Preserve its sky/cloud background and the full top navigation, including the exact original logo, links, button and their positions. Add an enormous ancient tree limb coming from off-screen RIGHT, seen close-up from underneath against this same sky. Photoreal nature photography. Landscape 16:10 2880x1800.
+COMPOSITION is critical: this is the RIGHT HALF of a website hero. Keep the ENTIRE LEFT 46% EMPTY SKY and leave a clear sky strip across the ENTIRE TOP 15% for navigation. The canopy must have natural irregular leaf edges below that top strip, not a straight cropped edge. Keep the bottom 8% empty too. The only edge touched by the tree is the RIGHT edge. Main thick woody entry meets the right edge at 30% image height; bark diameter is one quarter of image height (450px). Within a short distance it splits into FOUR heavy boughs spreading leftward and down like a hand, ending just right of the image's center (x1350). Use the whole right half: very massive, broad, dense, deep overlapping ivy foliage with dark inner mass and long curtains of hanging Spanish moss down to 87% height. Clustered small tree leaves, large foreground ivy leaves, fern epiphytes, very thick cushion moss on craggy bark as in references. Foliage fills much of the right half. No skinny single limb.
+Bright upper-right sky backlighting, translucent lime leaf rims, almost black blue-green inner foliage, cool blue bounced light on dark bark underside, top bark rim light, far left foliage hazier and softer. A few big optically blurred leaves at far right, 80-160px leaves close to lens. Fine hanging tendrils with slight motion. No ground, trunk base, watermark, other text, illustration, CGI or cutout halo. Do not move any navigation or add additional UI. The first image is the actual base; other references only show botanical textures. Classic version with FOUR forks, dense ivy, long hanging moss.
+
+02 Wide & heavy
+Edit the first reference screenshot using the SECOND reference as the guide for the tree's size, composition and atmospheric photography. The second image is approved variation 01. Make variation 02 distinctly WIDER, HEAVIER and DARKER with SIX huge woody forks rather than four and much denser clustered ivy/tree foliage. Keep the underlying FIRST screenshot pixel-unchanged. Keep the second image's branch entry high at upper-right, bark thickness approximately one quarter of picture height, preserve the leftmost extent around the picture midpoint. Fan six heavy boughs in a much broader, denser open-hand canopy from upper-right toward the center. Very dark blue-green inner leaf mass, radiant translucent lime rims, cool blue light reflected on underside bark. Chunky moss on deeply textured bark, epiphytic ferns, layered ivy. Right-edge big foreground leaves softly blurred. Ancient forest photography seen from below.
+Keep all canopy naturally contoured and completely BELOW a generous unbroken strip of blue sky containing ALL navigation and the button. No foliage anywhere behind the button or near the button shadow. Only the right edge cuts through the attached thick main limb. ALL moss and vine strands must END naturally inside the picture, longest at 88% of frame height with a generous empty bottom margin; no strand touches the bottom edge. Left 45% stays pure sky, all lower-left space clean. Layered canopy fills right half, heavy and immersive. No sun disk, no new clouds, no UI changes. Output single horizontal 16:10 image 2880x1800. Photoreal, no illustrations, no CGI, no halos.
+
+03 Airy
+EDIT Image 1, the original CERNAN sky screenshot. Image 2 shows the required massive scale and photographic quality of the tree, but make a distinctly AIRIER variation with different branch anatomy. Keep Image 1's sky/clouds/navigation unchanged; output 16:10 2880x1800.
+VARIATION 03 AIRY: Huge 420px thick moss-encrusted tree limb entering from offscreen right at upper third, branching into FOUR widely spaced thick arms with generous irregular windows of blue sky between leaf clusters. Still a huge close old limb, never skinny or sparse single branch. Right-half composition, farthest left twigs just RIGHT OF CENTER (52% width); entire left half is clean sky. Natural lush ivy clusters and smaller tree leaves, fine lace-like curtains of Spanish moss and delicate thin vertical hanging strands, longest to 85% frame height in the right half. The FOUR major limbs fan broadly left/up/down within a short distance of the right edge, each carries dense smaller clusters with open space BETWEEN clusters. A few tiny ferns in forks, rich living moss and rough detailed bark. Big softly blurred close leaves at far-right edge. Seen from BELOW, glowing upper-right backlight, lime translucent outer leaves, dark blue-green undersides and cool sky bounce on bark, far left tips softer and hazier.
+Keep generous empty sky band across top for all navigation and the meeting button, including button shadow. All plant silhouettes naturally contoured, not straight cutoffs. Only attached main branch and a few foreground leaves touch the RIGHT edge; nothing touches top/bottom/left. Hanging tips END fully inside the picture above an empty bottom margin. No ground, standing tree base, new text, CG, illustration, watermarks, halos or added sun disk.
+
+04 Low dip
+Edit the FIRST image (original CERNAN screenshot) into a photoreal website hero. Second image is a scale/realism guide only. Preserve exact original sky/clouds/nav. 16:10 horizontal 2880x1800.
+VARIATION04 LOW DIP: An immense old mossy tree limb enters horizontally from offscreen RIGHT, centered 36% from the top (y650 in1800px). The woody entry is 26% of frame height thick (470px). It quickly splits into FOUR heavy forks that sweep LEFT and sag in a low deep graceful curve. The lowest major limb dips around 55% frame height, then curves slightly upward at its far-left tip. Many smaller branches, dense lush ivy and tree-leaf clusters, heavy fern epiphytes and cushions of living moss. Many extra-long vines and Spanish moss curtains POUR DOWN from the sagging arms, uneven wispy endings, longest at 92% frame height (y1650), particularly toward the right. Farthest left canopy stops just right of image center; leave all left 46% pure sky. Huge broad weighty canopy seen from below and slightly left; old heavy wood must clearly dominate the right half, never slender isolated branch.
+Bright upper-right backlight, translucent lime rims, near-black blue-green shadowed leaf masses, cool blue reflected light on rough underside bark. Atmospheric fading at farthest left tips and subtle wind in long moss. A few big blurred close leaves at right edge. Top15% remains original empty sky and original navigation, full button and shadow unobstructed. No growth behind navigation. Everything including longest hanging tips ends above bottom edge. No ground, no trunk base, no new words, no render or illustration, no halos, no watermark.
+
+05 Upswept
+Edit Image1, the original CERNAN website sky screenshot, preserving exact sky, clouds and top navigation. Create one photoreal 16:10 2880x1800 image, variation05 UPSWEPT.
+One HUGE thick old tree limb enters from offscreen RIGHT with its woody centerline 26% down from top, diameter 25% of frame height. Within a short distance it forks into FIVE muscular curving limbs that sweep UPWARD and LEFT, forming a high arched canopy framing the upper-right. This is an upturned open hand seen from BELOW. Dense ivy and small tree-leaf clusters above and between the major limbs, mossy bark, large ferns in crooks, dramatic deep overlapping dark blue-green inner mass. Longest reach LEFT toward 42% of image width, but only in upper-middle (between 24% and36% of height). All canopy and hanging growth BELOW 39% height stays strictly in RIGHT 54% of picture. Left third completely empty sky. Substantial thick horizontally spreading limbs, not one skinny stick.
+Fewer hanging strands than other versions: select fine vertical moss curtains and trailing vines in the far RIGHT, longest down to 75% height, none in lower-left. Keep this canopy more elevated and upward-sweeping than a drooping tree. Entire TOP13% clear original sky and nav; maximum rise can approach top edge only at extreme right OUTSIDE and to the right of the meeting button, without ever touching button, shadow, text or logo. Huge 80-160px close leaves at right, a few softly out of focus. High upper-right backlight makes leaf edges glow translucent lime, underneath dark and cool, blue ambient light on rugged mossy bark. Distant left foliage soft hazy blue-green. No added sun disk, background changes, ground, rooted trunk, extra text, watermark, checkerboard or render look. Only the right edge cuts through branch; moss tips end naturally inside frame.
+
+06 Close-up
+IMAGE EDIT on first reference CERNAN website screenshot. Second reference is scale/layout guide. Keep the FIRST original blue gradient, clouds and full top navigation unchanged. One 16:10 2880x1800 image.
+VARIATION06 CLOSE-UP: camera is nearer, right-side ancient bough feels enormous and tactile, its bark dominates the immediate right foreground. Horizontal main limb enters OFFSCREEN RIGHT centered 28% height, diameter 28% of picture height (about500px). Splits rapidly into THREE very thick gnarled forks spreading broadly LEFT and up/down, then a thick multi-layer canopy of many smaller branches and dense real ivy/tree leaves. Far-left foliage reaches just before picture center (47% width), all left45% empty sky. Macro-level sharp detail on moss cushions, tiny moss shoots, rough corklike plates and fissures in near bark, delicate ferns growing from crooks. An oversized ivy leaf cluster at the immediate far-right edge is strongly defocused by shallow depth of field; adjacent bark remains sharp. Near leaves 80-160px, distant leaves smaller and hazier. Lots of long Spanish moss and ivy tendrils end near 85% height, on the right.
+Photoreal high-end nature camera, view from underneath and slightly left. Deep blue-green shadows, cool blue sky reflected on bark underside, upper-right sun creates glowing translucent lime leaf edges and fine bark rimlight. Dense atmospheric layers and real organic textures. Large volumetric foliage, not a sticker. Preserve clear sky around all original nav including meeting pill/shadow. Top14% empty sky, all hanging tips end inside frame, no flat cropped contours except where limb enters right. No ground, no soil/trunk base, no illustration, CGI, text, flare, halos or watermark.
+
+07 Drifting leaves
+Edit the first original CERNAN screenshot to make VARIATION07 DRIFTING LEAVES. Second image is the classic canopy to closely match. Preserve the exact original first screenshot background and nav. Single 16:10 landscape 2880x1800.
+Recreate the second image's HUGE classic mossy tree limb entering offscreen RIGHT in the upper third, with FOUR very thick wide-fanning forks, dense layered ivy and small tree leaves, abundant moss curtains and hanging vines down to 85% height, very dark blue-green interior, luminous lime leaf rims, ferns in crooks, cool sky bounce on bark, photographic haze on far-left twigs and big soft-focus foreground leaves cropped by far right. Main bark entry roughly quarter frame height thick. Main canopy remains in right half, far left canopy stops at 47% width. Entire top14% nav strip empty sky, full button/shadow clear, lower-left44% entirely empty.
+ADD EXACTLY EIGHT individual falling green leaves floating in otherwise empty sky BETWEEN 30% and52% image width and BETWEEN 22% and37% height. Scatter them irregularly with varied rotation, size and depth; a subtle suggestion of motion. They are clearly separate leaves, not attached vines, not dots, not symbols. Six to ten allowed, target eight. They must ALL be in that narrow UPPER-MIDDLE sky band, never below39% height on left or over nav. No leaves in bottom-left text area. Graceful natural breeze. No added words, sun disk, watermark, ground, illustration, CGI, halos. The branch is massive and layered, never a small sticker. Every hanging tip ends naturally inside frame.
+
+08 Old giant
+Edit the FIRST reference, original CERNAN website sky screenshot. Preserve the original sky, clouds, gradient and existing nav exactly. Image2 shows large scale/layout; Image3 botanical liana reference only, ignore its checkerboard and watermark. Output single photoreal 16:10 2880x1800.
+VARIATION08 OLD GIANT. A monumental centuries-old overhanging limb enters from OFFSCREEN RIGHT in the upper third, center29% height and wood diameter27% height. FOUR massive twisted and interwoven forks fan LEFT, up and down, broadening into a huge dense canopy across right half. Very old charcoal-brown bark with extraordinarily deep fissures, gnarled burls, corky ridges and spiraling growth. Thick rope-like woody lianas wrap around the giant bough and hang down in long loose vertical arcs. Several aerial roots hang freely in air, never touch soil or ground. Moss-encrusted branch tops, epiphytes, fern clumps, deep layered ivy/tree-leaf masses. Many hanging Spanish moss threads intermixed with distinctive thick twisted woody ropes. Longest hanging root/liana tips around 90% frame height in right half, all natural tips visible and ending inside frame.
+Seen close from UNDER and left. Upper-right backlight, intensely dark blue-green interior, glowing translucent lime leaf rims, cold blue reflected sky on dark bark underside, gentle warmer bark rimlight. Subtle atmospheric depth softens distant left foliage; big nearest leaves at far-right edge softly defocused. Main canopy never extends left of46% picturewidth, leaving left third and all lower-left completely clear. Generous clear sky band across top15% for unchanged CERNAN, Research FAQs Contact and full original meeting button/shadow. Only right edge cuts limb. No ground, standing trunk, dirt, added sun, new text, checkerboard, watermark, CG, illustration, white outlines or halos. Old, weighty, twisting organic architecture should clearly distinguish this image.
+
+09 Spring light
+EDIT THE FIRST IMAGE, the original CERNAN website screenshot. Keep its original sky-blue gradient, blurred clouds and all navigation exactly unchanged. Second image is a guide to the massive branch scale and right-side framing, not leaf color. Produce one photoreal 16:10 2880x1800 image.
+VARIATION09 SPRING LIGHT: A giant old mossy tree limb enters from offscreen RIGHT centered 28% height, wood diameter25% of frameheight, splitting immediately into FOUR or FIVE very thick curved forks fanning left/up/down and widening into a huge dense lush canopy. Fresh SPRING foliage, mostly luminous yellow-green and lime-green young leaves with translucent veins, mixed larger ivy leaves and small newly unfurled tree leaves. Bright fresh moss cushions, delicate new ferns and epiphytes in the crooks. Maintain real depth with cool dark blue-green internal shadows under the leaves and rough shadow-side bark. Strongest glowing upper-right backlight of the set, optimistic sunlit fresh growth, SOFTEST atmospheric haze at far-left tips, natural photographic softness. No actual sun disk, no white glow over background; the original sky plate stays unchanged. Dense layered plant masses, not scattered leaves. Many thin vertical hanging moss strands and ivy vines of varied lengths ending around85% pictureheight. A few large optically blurred close leaves at far right.
+Canopy restricted to right half, leftmost tips just before center around47% width. Left third and all lower-left44% pure sky. Entire top14% empty original sky and nav. Keep button plus shadow untouched with generous clearance. Only right edge intersects attached tree; hanging tips naturally end inside frame. Photograph viewed from below and slightly left with big near leaves and smaller hazier far leaves. No ground, treebase, soil, words, checkerboard, illustration, CG, halos or watermark.
+
+10 Layered depth
+Edit FIRST image, the original CERNAN website screenshot. Keep the exact original sky gradient, blurred clouds, and complete navigation with meeting button unchanged. SECOND image is the large foreground limb scale guide. Single 16:10 2880x1800 photo image.
+VARIATION10 LAYERED DEPTH: Show TWO distinct overhanging tree limbs at clearly different optical distances, both enter from OFFSCREEN RIGHT. Closest dominant limb has SHARP detailed fissured bark, thick moss, dense vivid layered ivy/tree-leaf clusters, ferns in forks. Woody attachment at right edge centered32% height, diameter26% height, quickly fans into FOUR thick arms sweeping left/up/down. It fills right half and reaches near47% width. Long sharp moss curtains and dangling vines hang from it to85-90% height. Close big leaves blur at immediate far-right edge.
+A SECOND SEPARATE limb is BEHIND and HIGHER than the foreground one, seen through an open band of sky between them. Rear limb centered around20% height, smaller due distance and extending leftward to48%width. It has distinctly softer focus, cool blue-green haze, reduced contrast, smaller leaves, fine mist-softened hanging strands. Must read as a second remote tree canopy, NOT just another sharp fork of front branch. Foreground fork partially overlaps and occludes rear limb on the right, with atmospheric gap revealing distance toward left. High-end nature photo viewed from underneath, strong parallax depth illusion. Vivid translucent lime-green leaf rims from high upper-right sun, deep blue-green inner shadows and cool sky bounce on the front bark. Rear layer is noticeably softer lighter and cooler.
+Entire left44% clean sky and ALL lower-left44% untouched. Entire TOP13% is clear original sky and original nav, keep BOTH limbs fully below the nav band and away from the complete meeting button and shadow. No foliage over logo or links. Every hanging tip ends inside image, only right border intersects woody limbs. No ground, upright trunk, illustration, CGI, added sun disk, checkerboard, new text, halos or watermark.
+

